    "description": "Period- and region-scoped historical given-name variants (diminutives, familiar forms, and scribal abbreviations) mapped to their formal forms. Serves fulltext_search and image_transcribe, which do not auto-expand names (record_search and external sites already expand — see issue #1868). English only in this file; the Latin/cognate cross-language need is deliberately OUT OF SCOPE for #1868 (see `out_of_scope` below).",
    "issue": "https://github.com/PioneerAIAcademy/cowork-genealogy/issues/1868",
    "shape": "per language -> per formal name -> { period, region, source, variants: [ { form, attested, source? } ] }. `attested` is per-VARIANT (not per formal name) so the measured/untested split is preserved exactly: only a variant with committed measured evidence is `attested: true`.",
    "attested_note": "Exactly three variant->formal pairs carry measured evidence: Betty->Elizabeth, Peggy->Margaret, Polly->Mary (membership test 8/8 over three name families, 2026-08-08). Every other variant is untested (attested: false) — present because it appears in the cited in-repo prose table, not because its reach was measured.",
    "sourcing": "Every entry traces to an in-repo file:line. No source is invented.",
    "out_of_scope": "Cross-language name forms — the inline cognates in the seed tables (Hans/Honza for John, Diego for James, Paco/Pepe for Francis/Joseph) and the Latin/Spanish/German block at search-strategies.md:76-83 (Joannes<->John, Iacobus<->James, Catalina<->Catherine, Wilhelm<->William, etc.) — are deliberately excluded. They are a different substitution mechanism (cross-language cognate / ecclesiastical register-form equivalence, formal<->formal across languages), not within-language diminutive expansion, and #1868 was scoped English-only on 2026-08-24 over one combined name-form table to keep issue #607's expansion contract to a single kind of substitution. Not tracked by a separate issue yet.",
